> What is it called when an arrest for drunk driving is left without a conviction?
**assistant**:
> When an arrest for drunk driving does not result in a conviction, it is often referred to as a "dismissal" or "case dismissal." This occurs when the charges are dropped before trial or when the case does not lead to a guilty verdict in court. In some instances, a plea bargain or completion of a diversion program may also result in the charges being dismissed without a formal conviction. It's important to note that the specifics can vary depending on the jurisdiction.
